l,47.5,null,null,48.0,null,null,48.5,null,null,49.0,null,null,49.5,null,null,50.0,null,null,50.5,null,null,51.0,null,null,51.5,null,null,52.0,null,null,52.5,null,null,53.0,null,null,53.5,null,null,54.0,null,null,54.5,null,null,55.0,null,null,55.5,null,null,56.0,null,null,56.5,null,null,57.0,null,null,57.5,null,null,58.0,null,null,58.5,null,null,59.0,null,null,59.5,null,null,60.0,null,null,60.5,null,null,61.0,null,null,61.5,null,null,62.0,null,null,62.5,null,null,63.0,null,null,63.5,null,null,64.0,null,null,64.5,null,null,65.0,null,null,65.5,null,null,66.0,null,null,66.5,null,null,67.0,null,null,67.5,null,null,68.0,null,null,68.5,null,null,69.0,null,null,69.5,null,null,70.0,null,null,70.5,null,null,71.0,null,null,71.5,null,null,72.0,null,null,72.5,null,null,73.0,null,null,73.5,null,null,74.0,null,null,74.5,null,null,75.0,null,null,75.5,null,null,76.0,null,null,76.5,null,null,77.0,null,null,77.5,null,null,78.0,null,null,78.5,null,null,79.0,null,null,79.5,null,null,80.0,null,null,80.5,null,null,81.0,null,null,81.5,null,null,82.0,null,null,82.5,null,null,83.0,null,null,83.5,null,null,84.0,null,null,84.5,null,null,85.0,null,null,85.5,null,null,86.0,null,null,86.5,null,null,87.0,null,null,87.5,null,null,88.0,null,null,88.5,null,null,89.0,null,null,89.5,null,null,90.0,null,null,90.5,null,null,91.0,null,null,91.5,null,null,92.0,null,null,92.5,null,null,93.0,null,null,93.5,null,null,94.0,null,null,94.5,null,null,95.0,null,null,95.5,null,null,96.0,null,null,96.5,null,null,97.0,null,null,97.5,null,null,98.0,null,null,98.5,null,null,99.0,null,null,99.5]}],"solution":"class UndergroundSystem:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.active = {}                 # id -> (startStation, startTime)\n        self.routes = defaultdict(lambda: [0, 0])   # (start, end) -> [totalTime, trips]\n\n    def checkIn(self, id: int, stationName: str, t: int) -> None:\n        self.active[id] = (stationName, t)\n\n    def checkOut(self, id: int, stationName: str, t: int) -> None:\n        start, t0 = self.active.pop(id)\n        route = self.routes[(start, stationName)]\n        route[0] += t - t0\n        route[1] += 1\n\n    def getAverageTime(self, startStation: str, endStation: str) -> float:\n        total, trips = self.routes[(startStation, endStation)]\n        return total / trips\n","approach":"**Key insight: an average only needs a running sum and a count, never the individual journeys.** Two hash maps do the whole job. `active` maps a passenger id to where and when they checked in; `checkOut` pops that entry, computes the duration and adds it to the `(start, end)` route's `[total, count]`. `getAverageTime` is a division.\n\nPopping on check-out both frees memory and lets the same passenger travel again. Keying routes by the ordered pair keeps A -> B separate from B -> A.\n\n**Common mistakes:** storing a list of durations per route and averaging on every query (O(trips) per query and unbounded memory); keying routes by an unordered pair; forgetting to remove the active check-in, which would leak memory over millions of passengers; integer division in languages where that matters.\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** Floating-point drift over billions of trips: keep the sum as an integer (or use Kahan summation) and divide only on read. Scaling: routes are independent, so shard by route key; the `active` map can live in a fast store keyed by passenger. Thread safety: updates to a route's sum and count must be atomic together (lock per route or a compare-and-swap on a packed struct). Also discuss handling a check-out without a matching check-in (data error) gracefully.","complexity":{"time":"O(1) per operation","space":"O(active passengers + distinct routes)"},"similar":["design-hit-counter","lru-cache"],"number":177}